  "nl_text": "The database schema named 'schemabench_0128' consists of three tables: 'businesses', 'inspections', and 'violations'.\nThe 'businesses' table is used to store information about various businesses. It includes columns for 'business_id', 'name', 'address', 'city', 'postal_code', 'latitude', 'longitude', 'phone_number', 'tax_code', 'business_certificate', 'application_date', 'owner_name', 'owner_address', 'owner_city', 'owner_state', and 'owner_zip'. These columns all allow null values except for 'name' and 'business_certificate' which are not null. The 'business_id' is the primary key for this table.\nThe 'inspections' table is used to store information about business inspections. It includes columns for 'business_id', 'score', 'date', and 'type'. The 'business_id' column is a foreign key referencing the 'businesses' table.\nThe 'violations' table is used to store information about business violations. It includes columns for 'business_id', 'date', 'violation_type_id', 'risk_category', and 'description'. The 'business_id' column is a foreign key referencing the 'businesses' table.\nThis schema ensures referential integrity by enforcing the constraints of foreign keys. When a record in the 'businesses' table is deleted, any corresponding records in the 'inspections' and 'violations' tables will also be deleted to maintain data integrity.",
  "gold_question": "Background / Context:\n\nThe project involves the development of a predictive analytics system for the San Francisco Department of Public Health. The system will manage data about food-related businesses, inspections, and violations. This involves predicting unscheduled inspection scores to ensure public health standards are maintained across eateries.\n\nObjectives:\n\n1. Predict inspection scores for unscheduled inspections from 2013 to 2016, with scores ranging from 1 to 100.\n2. Use historical data to enhance the Department's ability to forecast potential public health risks.\n\nStakeholders & Users:\n\n- San Francisco Department of Public Health officials\n- Data analysts and public health inspectors\n- Business owners affected by inspections\n\nFunctional Descriptions:\n\n1. Business Management:\n   - Store and manage data on businesses, including identification, location, and ownership details.\n   \n2. Inspection Record Keeping:\n   - Maintain a log of inspections, including scores, dates, and types.\n   - Facilitate the prediction of future inspection scores based on historical inspection data.\n\n3. Violation Tracking:\n   - Document violations, including type and risk category.\n   - Link violations to businesses and specific inspection events.\n\nNon-Functional Descriptions:\n\n- The system should ensure the confidentiality and integrity of business data.\n- Data processing should be efficient to allow timely predictions and analysis.\n- The solution must scale to handle a large volume of data spanning several years of records.",
  "input_json": "/data/SchemaBench/Experiment/schema2text_deepseek/0128.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: schemabench_0128\nCREATE TABLE `businesses` (\n  `business_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `address` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `city` varchar(100) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `postal_code` varchar(20) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `latitude` decimal(10,6) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `longitude` decimal(10,6) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `phone_number` varchar(20) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `tax_code` varchar(50) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `business_certificate` varchar(100) NOT NULL,\n  `application_date` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `owner_name` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `owner_address` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `owner_city` varchar(100) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `owner_state` varchar(100) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `owner_zip` varchar(20) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`business_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `inspections` (\n  `inspection_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `business_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `score` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `date` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `type` varchar(100) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`inspection_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `inspections_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`business_id`) REFERENCES `businesses` (`business_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `violations` (\n  `violation_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `business_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `date` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `violation_type_id` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `risk_category` varchar(100) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `description` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`violation_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `violations_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`business_id`) REFERENCES `businesses` (`business_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
